      "title": "School of Education",
      "description": "School of Education - Adjunct Faculty | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu School of Education - Adjunct Faculty To meet ongoing needs for part-time instructors, Lenoir-Rhyne University maintains adjunct candidate pools by areas of specialty to meet varying semester to semester needs. We encourage you to submit your application online (including attachments for your cover letter and your curriculum vitae). Your cover letter should focus specifically on your teaching experience and your philosophy of teaching. Also, please discuss how your specific expertise would match up to current courses or areas in our program. Review our current academic catalog on the Office of the Registrar page. According to our regional accreditation requirements, all college instructors should possess at least a Master's degree and at least 18 hours of completed graduate work in the specific field of study. Except in rare cases, Lenoir-Rhyne University will expect at least a Master's degree in the particular field of study in which the instructor is teaching. Your application materials will be maintained in our archives for at least 18 months. As your vitae changes, we encourage you to update your application by re-submitting your materials. Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff, and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation, and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. Contact Information First and Last Name Email Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload Curriculum Vitae One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload cover letter and curriculum vitae Files should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format if possible. Use the \"Choose File\" button to find the files on your computer, and then click Submit. Please do not use special characters in the file names of your cover letter and CV such as commas, accented letters, etc. The only acceptable special characters are hyphens, underscores, and periods. Example: INCORRECT: Doe, John.docx CORRECT: Doe-John.docx or Doe_John.docx Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University Use of personal data and cookies This website uses cookies to improve your experience. Data Privacy Statement OK May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
