    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr/part-time-faculty-school-of-hess": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, School of Health, Exercise and Sport Science",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, School of Health, Exercise and Sport Science | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Part-time Faculty, School of Health, Exercise and Sport Science Location: Hickory, North Carolina The School of Health, Exercise and Sport Science (HESS) faculty have primary responsibility for  implementation of educational curriculum, facilitation of all aspects of student learning in the classroom. To meet ongoing needs for part-time instructors, Lenoir-Rhyne University (LR) maintains adjunct candidate pools by areas of specialty to meet the needs for the programs. Programs offered in the School of HESS include B.S. in Exercise Science, B.S. in Public Health, B.A. in Sports Management, M.S. Exercise Science, Master of Public Health, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) and M.S. in Occupational Therapy. The School of HESS also offers courses that support the Health and Wellness component of the General Education, including various activity courses. All positions are based on enrollment and subject to available funding. Type of Appointment Faculty: Adjunct Faculty Position Location School of Health Exercise and Sport Science, Hickory campus, in person Reporting Lenoir-Rhyne University School of Health Exercise and Sport Science, Chair Essential Faculty Duties and Responsibilities Contribute to student instruction and evaluation as course coordinator, lecturer, laboratory instructor and/or small group discussion facilitator in areas appropriate to specialty, clinical experience and educational preparation, including actively taking part in assuring the availability of remedial instruction as assigned by the Program Director Qualifications Required Master’s degree or at a minimum 18 hours of completed graduate work toward the specific field or area for undergraduate instruction Required Master’s degree in the specific field or area of study for graduate instruction Preferred prior teaching experience in the specific field or area of study Application materials will be maintained in our archives for at least 18 months. As your vitae changes, we encourage you to update your application by re-submitting your materials. Behavioral Expectations Maintain high integrity, confidentiality and ethical standards Maintain a healthy and safe environment Maintain and contribute to a professional, respectful, courteous and inclusive environment Treat other individuals with dignity, respect and kindness Adhere to all university policies, procedures, standards, values and comply with all federal state, and local laws Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff, and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation, and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. About Lenoir-Rhyne University Lenoir-Rhyne University is a co-educational, private masters comprehensive liberal arts institution founded in 1891, with its traditional campus located in Hickory, N.C., a town of more than 40,000. The university has additional off-campus instructional sites in Asheville, N.C. and Columbia, S.C. The university now offers more than 50 undergraduate and 20 graduate degree programs to approximately 2,400 students. Lenoir-Rhyne University seeks to liberate mind and spirit, clarify personal faith, foster physical wholeness, build a sense of community, and promote responsible leadership for service in the world. Affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), Lenoir-Rhyne promotes campuses open to people from all religious and non-religious backgrounds. About College of Health Sciences The College of Health Sciences at Lenoir-Rhyne University provides current and practical knowledge and skills that prepares students for success in differing health science careers. The college offers four undergraduate degrees: Exercise Science, Nursing, Public Health, and Sports Management. At the graduate level the college offers: Master of Science Exercise Science, Master of Public Health, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) and Master of Science Occupational Therapy. Apply Name First Name Last Name Email Application Documents Upload Curriculum Vitae One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload Letter of Application One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University Use of personal data and cookies This website uses cookies to improve your experience. Data Privacy Statement OK May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr/college-humanities-and-social-sciences-adjunct-faculty-asheville": {
      "title": "College of Humanities and Social Sciences",
      "description": "College of Humanities and Social Sciences - Adjunct Faculty, Asheville | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu College of Humanities and Social Sciences - Adjunct Faculty, Asheville Position based at Asheville, N.C. campus. Please note: The College of Humanities and Social Sciences includes the following undergraduate and graduate programs: American studies, criminal justice, German, history, human and community services, philosophy, politics and international affairs, political science, politics and law, psychology, religious studies, sociology, and Spanish. To meet ongoing needs for part-time instructors, Lenoir-Rhyne University maintains adjunct candidate pools by areas of specialty to meet varying semester to semester needs. We encourage you to submit your application online (including attachments for your cover letter and your curriculum vitae). Your cover letter should focus specifically on your teaching experience and your philosophy of teaching. Also, please discuss how your specific expertise would match up to current courses or areas in our program. Review our current academic catalog on the Office of the Registrar page. According to our regional accreditation requirements, all college instructors should possess at least a Master's degree and at least 18 hours of completed graduate work in the specific field-of-study. Except in rare cases, Lenoir-Rhyne University will expect at least a Master's degree in the particular field-of-study in which the instructor is teaching. Your application materials will be maintained in our archives for at least 18 months. As your vitae changes, we encourage you to update your application by re-submitting your materials. Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff, and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation, and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. Contact Information First and Last Name Email Discipline American Studies Criminal Justice French German History Human and Community Services Philosophy Political Science/Politics/International Affairs/Law Psychology Religious Studies Sociology Spanish Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload Curriculum Vitae One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload cover letter and curriculum vitae Files should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format if possible. Use the \"Choose File\" button to find the files on your computer, and then click Submit. Please do not use special characters in the file names of your cover letter and CV such as commas, accented letters, etc. The only acceptable special characters are hyphens, underscores, and periods. Example: INCORRECT: Doe, John.docx CORRECT: Doe-John.docx or Doe_John.docx Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University Use of personal data and cookies This website uses cookies to improve your experience. Data Privacy Statement OK May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
