ss at least a Master's degree and at least 18 hours of completed graduate work in the specific field-of-study. Except in rare cases, Lenoir-Rhyne University will expect at least a Master's degree in the particular field-of-study in which the instructor is teaching. Your application materials will be maintained in our archives for at least 18 months. As your vitae changes, we encourage you to update your application by re-submitting your materials. Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff, and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation, and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. Contact Information First and Last Name Email Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload Curriculum Vitae One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf  doc. Upload cover letter and curriculum vitae Files should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format if possible. Use the \"Choose File\" button to find the files on your computer, and then click Submit. Please do not use special characters in the file names of your cover letter and CV such as commas, accented letters, etc. The only acceptable special characters are hyphens, underscores, and periods. Example: INCORRECT: Doe, John.docx CORRECT: Doe-John.docx or Doe_John.docx Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Maga