    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr/assistant-director-financial-aid": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Assistant Director of Financial Aid Location : Hickory, North Carolina The successful candidate will demonstrate strong knowledge and understanding of federal, state and institutional financial aid policies and processes, initiative, creative problem-solving, strong analytical skills, meticulous attention to detail, positive energy and a sense of humor. The successful candidate must demonstrate the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, deadline-oriented work environment while managing multiple responsibilities concurrently. Supervisory Responsibilities None Essential Duties and Responsibilities Administer federal, state, private and institutional financial aid programs on a daily basis. Manage the processing of federal, state, private and institutional financial aid through PowerFAIDS and applicable federal and state systems. Manage the processing, certification and reconciliation of state financial aid through North Carolina grant portals. Counsel students, parents and legal guardians regarding the availability of and eligibility requirements for Title IV, state and institutional financial aid. Counsel service members, in coordination with the VA Benefits Coordinator, regarding the availability of and eligibility requirements for Title IV, state and institutional financial aid. Manage projects and ongoing activities assigned by the Director or Associate Director of Financial Aid. Assist with short- and long-range planning to support efficient office operations and workflow. Respond promptly to questions and concerns from internal and external constituents, with the expectation that responses will be provided within one business day. Foster a positive and professional environment by ensuring all interactions reflect a commitment to exceptional customer service. Provide operational oversight of assigned financial aid functions to ensure accurate, timely and compliant administration of financial aid programs. Maintain proficiency in standard enrollment procedures as they relate to financial aid eligibility. Maintain current knowledge of applicable federal and state financial aid regulations and institutional policies to ensure ongoing compliance and accurate administration of financial aid programs. Provide leadership, training and guidance to campus stakeholders regarding financial aid eligibility, awarding and financial literacy. Assist with the preparation and submission of federal and state reports and surveys, as well as departmental statistical reports and projections. Assist with the periodic review, development and revision of departmental policies and procedures. Demonstrate a strong work ethic, attention to detail, and the ability to prioritize responsibilities effectively. Serve on university and division committees as appropriate. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Exceptional computer skills: PowerFAIDS experience preferred Exceptional verbal and written communication skills. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality Demonstrated planning, organizational and time-management skills. Ability to think strategically, manage multiple priorities, and adapt to changing demands Excellent team-building, customer service and leadership skills. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree required A minimum of three years of related experience. Knowledge of North Carolina state financial aid programs, including eligibility requirements, processing, certification, reconciliation and reporting, is preferred. Behavioral Expectations Maintain high integrity, confidentiality, and ethical standards. Maintain a healthy and safe environment. Maintain and contribute to a professional, respectful, courteous, diverse, equitable, and inclusive environment Treat other individuals with dignity, respect, and kindness. Adhere to all university policies, procedures, standards, values, and comply with all federal, state, and local laws. Position requirements in the role description outlined above indicate the minimum level of knowledge, skills, and/or abilities deemed necessary to perform the job competently. Role descriptions are an overview of the duties, responsibilities, and requirements of the position and are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list for the position. Employees may be required to perform other job-related assignments as requested and acquire new skills and responsibilities. Lenoir-Rhyne University reserves the right to modify, add, remove, or waive the responsibilities, duties, and skills required of the position. Application Process While completing the application, candidates will be prompted to submit: Resume Cover letter Three professional references References will only be contacted for finalists, and candidates will be notified in advance. The university’s mission, vision, and values statements may be reviewed using About LR . Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. About Lenoir-Rhyne University Lenoir-Rhyne University is a co-educational, private, comprehensive institution founded in 1891, with its traditional campus located in Hickory, North Carolina, a city of more than 40,000. The university has additional graduate centers in Asheville, N.C., and Columbia, S.C. Situated in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains, Lenoir- Rhyne is less than an hour’s drive from Charlotte, and the Hickory-Lenoir-Morganton Metropolitan Statistical Area has a population of about 365,000. The university now offers more than 45 undergraduate and 20 graduate degree programs to approximately 2,400 students. Lenoir-Rhyne University seeks to liberate mind and spirit, clarify personal faith, foster physical wholeness, build community, and promote responsible leadership for service to the world. Affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), Lenoir-Rhyne is open to people from all religious and non-religious backgrounds. Non-Discrimination and Equal Opportunity Policy Lenoir-Rhyne University is committed to providing a workplace and educational environment, as well as other benefits, programs, and activities that are free from discrimination, harassment and retaliation. LR is committed to creating a safe campus environment for all members of the LR community, including, but not limited to, those who identify as transgender and gender non-conforming. To that end, LR does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including sex stereotypes and sex characteristics), ethnicity, national origin, physical or mental disability, age, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status or any other characteristic or status protected by applicable law. To ensure compliance with federal and state civil rights laws and regulations and to affirm its commitment to promoting the goals of fairness and equity in all aspects of the educational program, activity and employment, LR has developed internal policies and procedures that provide a prompt, fair and impartial process for those involved in an allegation of discrimination or harassment, and for allegations of retaliation. LR values and upholds the equal dignity of all members of its community and strives to balance the rights of the parties in the grievance process during what is often a difficult time for all those involved. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Apply Name First Last Email Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Upload Three Professional References One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: txt rtf pdf doc docx odt ppt pptx odp xls xlsx ods. Upload Resume One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
    },
    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr/assistant-vice-president-university-hospitality-and-auxiliary-services": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for University Hospitality and Auxiliary Services",
      "description": "Assistant Vice President for University Hospitality and Auxiliary Services | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Assistant Vice President for University Hospitality and Auxiliary Services The Assistant Vice President for University Hospitality and Auxiliary Services is a senior administrator in the Office of the President who reports directly to the President. The AVP provides strategic and operational leadership for Conference and Event Services, Presidential Events, Enrollment Management events, the University Bookstore and Spirit Store, as well as campus dining, catering, and athletic concessions. The AVP brings these highly visible functions together to deliver exceptional hospitality, reliable service, strong business performance, and consistent stewardship of the Lenoir-Rhyne brand. The position strengthens the experience of students, employees, families, alumni, donors, trustees, fans, and guests while developing revenue opportunities that support the University’s mission. Organizational Role Working across divisional boundaries, the AVP coordinates the people, services, and resources needed to deliver campus-wide hospitality, auxiliary operations and university events. Key partners include Advancement and Alumni Engagement, Athletics, Enrollment Management, Student Experience, Finance and Administration, Facilities, Marketing and Communications, Campus Safety, academic units, and external hospitality and retail partners. The AVP advises the President on portfolio priorities, service concerns, business opportunities, and operational performance. The role provides leadership within its assigned portfolio and coordinates with partner units through established University policies and decision-making authority. Core Responsibilities Auxiliary Services Strategy Develop an integrated strategy and annual operating plans for hospitality, auxiliary services and University events that advance institutional priorities, improve the campus experience, and strengthen financial performance. Establish service standards, operating procedures, budgets, and performance measures; use customer feedback, operating data, and peer practices to guide improvements. Identify opportunities to expand services and use University facilities effectively while protecting academic priorities and the needs of the campus community. Conference and Event Services Lead Conference and Event Services department to manage planning, scheduling, and execution of events involving multiple departments, facilities, and service providers. Grow external conferences, camps, meetings, retreats, weddings, and other appropriate uses of University facilities; develop pricing, service packages, facility-use standards, and client relationships. Coordinate facilities, technology, catering, security, parking, housekeeping, and other event needs. Establish clear responsibilities, timelines, contingency plans, and post-event reviews. Presidential and Signature University Events Lead planning and execution of events hosted by the President, including receptions, dinners, trustee functions, donor and alumni gatherings, community events, and other institutional occasions. Provide event support for Opening Meeting, President’s Cookout, Commencement, Homecoming, donor celebrations, and other signature University events as assigned, in partnership with the responsible offices. Ensure careful attention to protocol, guest experience, accessibility, presentation, University traditions, and confidential information. Coordinate vendors and event teams to deliver consistent quality. Coordinates with the Executive Assistant in the Office of the President on all presidential events and activities Campus Dining Services Serve as the University’s principal institutional relationship manager for the campus food service vendor and oversee campus dining and catering performance against contractual and service expectations. Monitor food quality, service responsiveness, dining participation, meal-plan performance, financial results, and customer feedback; work with campus food service vendor and Student Experience to improve the student dining experience. Establish expectations for catering quality, presentation, timeliness, and hospitality for presidential functions, campus departments, Athletics, conferences, and external clients. Coordinate with appropriate partners on dietary needs, accessible service, food safety expectations, and corrective action when service or contract requirements are not met. University Bookstore and Spirit Store Oversee University Bookstore and Spirit Store operations and contracted retail relationships, as applicable; monitor service quality, inventory strategy, financial results, and customer satisfaction. Expand access to Lenoir-Rhyne apparel and merchandise through campus, online, game-day, event, and pop-up retail opportunities. Coordinate brand and trademark standards with Athletics and Marketing and Communications. Athletic Concessions and Game-Day Hospitality Partner with Athletics and service providers to oversee concessions and related hospitality, including offerings, pricing, staffing, presentation, service speed, and planning for high-attendance events. Improve the fan experience and concession revenue while maintaining appropriate food safety, cash-handling, and University operating standards. Revenue Generation and Business Performance Develop and manage assigned budgets; establish annual goals for revenue, expenses, margins, facility utilization, and service performance in collaboration with Finance. Identify and evaluate opportunities in conferences, rentals, catering, retail, concessions, and other auxiliary activities, considering demand, costs, staffing, capacity, and mission alignment. Review and negotiate contracts with Finance, Procurement, and University counsel as appropriate, following University approval and signature authority. Hold partners accountable for commitments, service levels, and corrective actions. Maintain appropriate internal controls and provide the President with regular financial and operating reports that identify trends, risks, results, and recommended action. University-Wide Service Excellence Champion a welcoming, responsive culture of hospitality across the University. Develop shared service expectations and training with partner offices to improve the experience of students and guests. Create effective channels for feedback, resolve complex service issues, and use recurring concerns to improve operations. Clarify ownership and escalation procedures across departments and vendors. Ensure events and auxiliary services reflect Lenoir-Rhyne’s mission, values, traditions, and brand; coordinate with appropriate offices on accessibility, safety, and emergency planning. Supervisory Responsibilities Directly supervise Conference and Event Services staff and other auxiliary-services personnel as assigned. Recruit, develop, coach, and evaluate staff; establish clear goals, appropriate staffing plans, and accountability for service and results. Provide institutional oversight of contracted providers through their designated management teams and contract terms. Contractor personnel remain under the supervision of their employers. Build productive working relationships among University staff, vendors, student employees, and event personnel. Leadership Competencies Hospitality and service excellence. Creates welcoming experiences and responds thoughtfully to diverse student and guest needs. Business and financial acumen. Uses budgets, operating data, and sound judgment to balance service quality with financial sustainability. Entrepreneurial thinking. Develops practical revenue opportunities aligned with institutional priorities and capacity. Operational leadership. Anticipates details, establishes reliable systems, and delivers complex events and services consistently. Collaboration and relationship management. Builds trust, influences across organizational boundaries, and holds partners accountable. Judgment and brand stewardship. Exercises discretion, communicates clearly, and represents the University with professionalism. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Significant progressively responsible experience in auxiliary services, hospitality, event management, conference services, dining, retail, business operations, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to lead staff and manage complex events and operations involving multiple stakeholders. Strong financial and business acumen, including budgeting, financial analysis, and revenue generation or business performance improvement. Experience managing contracts, external vendors, and service performance expectations. Excellent organizational, project-management, interpersonal, and written and verbal communication skills; ability to collaborate with senior leaders and across a complex organization. Demonstrated commitment to hospitality and customer service, sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to manage competing priorities. Availability for evening and weekend work as required by University events and operations. Preferred Qualifications Experience overseeing auxiliary services in higher education and managing outsourced dining, bookstore, or other major institutional service contracts. Experience supporting presidential, executive, trustee, donor, or other high-profile events. Demonstrated success growing revenue-producing conferences, camps, events, retail, or hospitality operations. Experience with collegiate athletic concessions and game-day hospitality. Measures of Success Annual goals and targets will be established with the President and appropriate University partners. Performance will be assessed through: Well-executed presidential and signature events, delivered within approved budgets and with strong stakeholder feedback. Measurable improvement in student, guest, and customer satisfaction and timely resolution of service concerns. Growth in appropriate external-event activity, facility utilization, and auxiliary revenue, with disciplined expense management and sustainable margins. Consistent fulfillment of Harvest Table and other vendor contract obligations and service standards. Effective cross-unit coordination, staff development, reliable reporting, and consistent presentation of the Lenoir-Rhyne brand. Working Environment Work takes place in office, dining, retail, athletic, and indoor and outdoor event settings and requires regular on-site presence. Evening and weekend work is required for major University, presidential, conference, and athletic events. The role involves moving among venues, adapting to changing schedules, and responding promptly to operational needs. Essential functions may be performed with reasonable accommodation. Application Process While completing the application, candidates will be prompted to submit: Resume Cover letter Three professional references References will only be contacted for finalists, and candidates will be notified in advance. The university’s mission, vision, and values statements may be reviewed using About LR . Lenoir-Rhyne University promotes a welcoming campus environment that is integral to the university's commitment to excellence in engagement and education. We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated experience nurturing a welcoming community, working with faculty, staff and/or students from all walks of life and/or incorporating varied perspectives and traditions in their current or previous positions. This commitment is rooted in our Lutheran tradition of fostering wisdom, nurturing vocation and preparing students for lives of purpose while serving the common good. Division: Office of the President Reports to: President Classification: Full-Time, Exempt Apply Name First Last Email Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Upload Three Professional References One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: txt rtf pdf doc docx odt ppt pptx odp xls xlsx ods. Upload Resume One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
    },
    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr/payroll-and-benefits-specialist-26": {
      "title": "Payroll and Benefits Specialist",
      "description": "Payroll and Benefits Specialist | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Payroll and Benefits Specialist Location: Hickory, NC The Payroll & Benefits Specialist is responsible for the accurate and timely administration of payroll and employee benefits for faculty, staff and student workers at Lenoir-Rhyne University, in compliance with applicable federal and state regulations, university policies and internal procedures. Working under the general direction of the Director of Human Resources and in collaboration with Finance, this position manages payroll and benefits as a combined function and serves as a primary point of contact for payroll-related inquiries. This position assists in aligning data between LR and third-party vendors, including benefit enrollments, payroll deductions, carrier invoices and compliance reporting. It also leads payroll and benefits audits and W-2 reporting while supporting a positive employee service experience. Lenoir-Rhyne University is committed to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment where students, faculty and staff experience a strong sense of belonging. The Payroll & Benefits Specialist is expected to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Process biweekly and monthly payroll cycles accurately and within established deadlines for all employee groups. Review, audit and reconcile payroll data, including timesheets, leave balances, earnings, deductions, tax withholdings and approvals, to ensure accuracy and compliance before final submission. Maintain payroll records, including new hires, terminations, compensation changes, tax elections and benefit deductions, while ensuring the confidentiality of sensitive information. Process garnishments, tax levies, child support orders and other involuntary deductions accurately and in a timely manner. Administer benefit enrollments, changes and terminations, including those related to new hires and qualifying life events, and ensure accurate payroll deductions. Review monthly carrier and vendor invoices against enrollment and payroll deduction data, resolve discrepancies with carriers and payroll, and approve invoices for payment. Administer COBRA and required benefit compliance notices in coordination with the vendor. Support annual open enrollment plan updates and employee engagement initiatives. Coordinate with HR and Finance colleagues to ensure payroll deductions, leave accruals, benefit changes and employment status changes are accurately reflected in payroll processing. Validate and approve annual W-2 reporting, year-end payroll activities, government reporting and required payroll filings in conjunction with the HRIS vendor. Conduct payroll and benefits audits to confirm that enrollment and dependent information are accurate, and prepare audit and compliance reports as requested. Partner with Finance on annual audits and requests related to payroll activity for general ledger and tax reporting. Perform HRIS/payroll audits, maintain internal controls and ensure data integrity, reporting accuracy and regulatory compliance. Maintain organized electronic payroll and benefits records and supports internal and external audits as needed. Respond to employee inquiries regarding pay, taxes, deductions, direct deposit, leave balances and benefits with professionalism, accuracy and confidentiality. Evaluate, recommend and implement improvements to payroll and benefits processes, reporting accuracy and employee service delivery. Maintain current knowledge of payroll and benefits regulations, systems and best practices to support accurate processing and compliance. Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Working knowledge of payroll practices, wage and hour regulations, and payroll tax procedures. Working knowledge of benefits administration, including eligibility and enrollment rules, and of FLSA, FMLA, ACA, ERISA and COBRA requirements. Strong attention to detail and high level of accuracy. Demonstrated ability to manage strict payroll deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. Analytical skills and the ability to create useful, actionable reports from HRIS data. Strong organizational, analytical and customer service skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively across departments and with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree required. A minimum of three to five years of payroll processing, HRIS administration and benefits administration experience is required; an equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Strong understanding of payroll and benefits regulations and compliance requirements. Experience with benefit deduction reconciliation and carrier invoice review required. Experience supporting multi-state payroll operations preferred. Experience with Paycom or a comparable HRIS/payroll platform preferred. Experience with benefit deduction reconciliation and administration preferred. Higher education or similarly complex multi-entity payroll experience preferred. CPP, CEBS, SHRM-CP or PHR certification, or progress toward certification, is preferred. Physical Requirements Prolonged periods of sitting and working at a computer and standard office equipment. Occasional lifting of files or office materials up to 15 pounds. Work Schedule Standard office hours are Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.-5 p.m. Occasional extended hours may be required during payroll processing periods, year-end activities, or open enrollment cycles. Behavioral Expectations Maintain high integrity, confidentiality, and ethical standards. Maintain a healthy and safe environment. Maintain and contribute to a professional, respectful, courteous, diverse, equitable, and inclusive environment Treat other individuals with dignity, respect, and kindness. Adhere to all university policies, procedures, standards, values, and comply with all federal, state, and local laws. Position requirements in the role description outlined above indicate the minimum level of knowledge, skills, and/or abilities deemed necessary to perform the job competently. Role descriptions are an overview of the duties, responsibilities, and requirements of the position and are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list for the position. Employees may be required to perform other job-related assignments as requested and acquire new skills and responsibilities. Lenoir-Rhyne University reserves the right to modify, add, remove, or waive the responsibilities, duties, and skills required of the position. About Lenoir-Rhyne University Lenoir-Rhyne University is a co-educational, private, comprehensive liberal arts institution founded in 1891, with its traditional campus located in Hickory, North Carolina, a city of more than 40,000. The university has additional graduate centers in Asheville, N.C., and Columbia, S.C. Situated in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains, Lenoir-Rhyne is less than an hour’s drive from Charlotte, and the Hickory-Lenoir-Morganton Metropolitan Statistical Area has a population of about 365,000. The university now offers more than 45 undergraduate and 20 graduate degree programs to approximately 2,400 students. Lenoir-Rhyne University seeks to liberate mind and spirit, clarify personal faith, foster physical wholeness, build community, and promote responsible leadership for service to the world. Affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), Lenoir-Rhyne is open to people from all religious and non-religious backgrounds. Non-Discrimination and Equal Opportunity Policy Lenoir-Rhyne University is committed to providing a workplace and educational environment, as well as other benefits, programs, and activities that are free from discrimination, harassment and retaliation. LR is committed to creating a safe campus environment for all members of the LR community, including, but not limited to, those who identify as transgender and gender non-conforming. To that end, LR does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including sex stereotypes and sex characteristics), ethnicity, national origin, physical or mental disability, age, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status or any other characteristic or status protected by applicable law. To ensure compliance with federal and state civil rights laws and regulations and to affirm its commitment to promoting the goals of fairness and equity in all aspects of the educational program, activity and employment, LR has developed internal policies and procedures that provide a prompt, fair and impartial process for those involved in an allegation of discrimination or harassment, and for allegations of retaliation. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Apply Contact Information First Name Last Name Email Documentation Upload Cover Letter One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Upload Resume One file only. 256 MB limit. Allowed types: pdf doc docx. Submit Leave this field blank Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
    }
  },
